{"name":"Fiddlehead Fern","hex":"#c8c387","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fiddlehead","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The scroll-shaped decoration at the tip of a fiddle.","A similar scroll-shaped ornament on a ship's bow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fiddlehead"},{"term":"fern","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of a group of some twenty thousand species of vascular plants classified in the division Pteridophyta that lack seeds and reproduce by shedding spores to initiate an alternation of generations.","A light green color inspired by the color of ferns."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fern"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fiddlehead","blocks":[{"text":"Fiddleheads or fiddlehead greens are the furled fronds from a fledgling fern, harvested for use as a vegetable."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Fiddlehead_closeup.png/330px-Fiddlehead_closeup.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fiddlehead"},{"title":"Fern","blocks":[{"text":"Ferns are a group of vascular plants that reproduce via spores and have neither seeds nor flowers. They reproduce in two phases, a short-lived gametophyte that reproduces sexually to develop a spore-bearing leaf structure. Some ferns produce coiled fiddleheads, which expand into fronds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/The_ferns_of_Great_Britain%2C_and_their_allies_the_club-mosses%2C_pepperworts%2C_and_horsetails_%28Pl._2%29_%288515393495%29.jpg/330px-The_ferns_of_Great_Britain%2C_and_their_allies_the_club-mosses%2C_pepperworts%2C_and_horsetails_%28Pl._2%29_%288515393495%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fern"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Pan_Roasted_Chicken_Breasts%2C_Garlic_Mashed_Potat